@executable @cli @assets @scaffold
Feature: An older tree upgrades to exactly the expected changes

  WHY. A release changes some files, adds some and retires some. A project generated by the
  previous release must, after `update`, hold exactly what a fresh `init` would, and the update
  must have touched exactly the files that changed. The previous tree is the committed baseline,
  rebuilt with a real lock, so 207 can show that an old tree run through new code changes nothing
  (ADR-006 §3, §4).

  Background:
    Given scenario "upgrade" of lane "work-update" names base "work-init/default"
    And its one step is "work update --json"

  Rule: R3 · A tree from an older baseline updates to exactly the expected changes

    Scenario: a committed baseline rebuilds into a tree update accepts as current
      Given the committed "work-init/default" baseline is rebuilt into a temp project
      Then every placeholder holds the running value: no "<project>", "<home>", "<timestamp>", "<version>" or "sha256:<hash>" remains
      And every lock entry's hash equals the hash of the rebuilt file it names
      And "work update --json" over it reports every planned file skipped

    Scenario Outline: each older-release mutation draws exactly its own action
      Given the rebuilt "work-init/default" tree with <mutation>
      When "work update --json" runs over it
      Then the step reports "<action>" for "<path>" and "skip" for every other planned file
      And afterwards "<path>" <after>

      Examples:
        | example | mutation                                                                            | action | path                              | after                         |
        | E7      | one line of older text in the file, and its lock hash matching that text            | update | .claude/commands/aof/refine.md    | equals the baseline's         |
        | E8      | the file present with "old\n", and a lock entry for command "retired"              | delete | .claude/commands/aof/retired.md   | does not exist                |
        | E9      | the file removed from disk and its entry removed from the lock                      | create | .claude/agents/aof-qa.md          | equals the baseline's         |

    Scenario: E10 · all three together update to exactly the expected changes and end on default
      When the harness compares scenario "upgrade" in lane "work-update"
      Then it passes
      And its step record's summary is 1 created, 1 updated, 1 deleted, 0 drift-warning and the rest skipped
      And its stored delta holds "steps.golden" and no project file

    Scenario Outline: a baseline whose lock records drift is not rebuilt
      Given <baseline>
      When it is rebuilt
      Then the rebuild fails naming the scenario and <path>
      And nothing is written

      Examples:
        | example | baseline                                                                             | path                                |
        | E11     | the committed "work-update/customised-update", whose step reports a drift-warning    | ".claude/commands/aof/refine.md"     |
        |         | a baseline whose lock names a file the baseline does not hold                       | the path the lock names              |
